<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Astrakhan Khanate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1466–1556</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Astrakhan Khanate was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> state on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a>, centred on the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astrakhan">Astrakhan</a>, that emerged from the break-up of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> in the fifteenth century. It controlled trade routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV of Russia</a> conquered it in 1556, bringing the whole course of the Volga under Muscovite rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/astrakhan-khanate.jpg" alt="Astrakhan Khanate" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Untifler assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Astrakhan_Khanate_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
